jobs.description:
Remote Executive Protection Intelligence Analyst

Pay rate: $37.03/hour

Schedule: Rotating schedule

We are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented **Executive Protection Intelligence Analyst** to join our dynamic, remote team. In this role, you will play a critical part in safeguarding our personnel and assets by providing real-time operational support, crisis management, and deep-dive risk analysis.

* 2 years experience working in a GSOC, fusion center, or equivalent
* Excellent knowledge of Windows or Mac computer operation, including Microsoft Office and G-Suite products;
* Experience conducting deep-dive OSINT investigations into suspicious activity.
* Ability to work and multitask in a fast-paced work environment, across multiple platforms, departments, time zones, and cultures;
* Experience producing analytical reports and briefs for stakeholders;
* Familiarity with open-source intelligence (OSINT), deep and dark web intelligence, physical security threats, and risk analysis concepts;
* Proficiency in crisis management and real-time operational support;
* Ability to assess and evaluate information and situations quickly and accurately, and to identify critical issues;
* Possess knowledge of threat assessment principles, including behavioral indicators and escalation pathways;
* Experience working with highly confidential and sensitive information;
* Excellent oral and written communication skills in English;
* Excellent customer service;
* Focused, organized, and detail-oriented;
* A desire to work as a dependable, participating team player with a positive attitude;
* A willingness to work varied shift hours, including overnights, weekends and holidays;
* Limited travel may be required

Preferred/Plus:

* Relevant GSOC experience in lieu of a degree is preferred;
* Customer service experience is preferred;
* Residing in the vicinity of an Uber Office (NY, DC, SF, Dallas, Chicago, Seattle) is preferred
* Experience with threat assessment/analysis is a plus;
* Fluency in additional languages is a plus;
* Experience with different communication platforms and technologies

**We service our clients best when we serve our employees first**

**United Security Inc. is one of the fastest growing security services companies in the USA. For over 31 years we work with clients from Boston to Miami and as far west as Texas. The last 5 years our revenue has grown by 140%! As a result of our incredible success, our goal is to continue accelerating our growth. We are looking for talent that will promote and adhere to the core values** ***(People, Integrity, Development and Community)*** **of United Security, Inc. The ideal candidate for a role at USI regularly exhibits support, commitment, good judgment, potential for growth, and goodwill.**

**If you appreciate having a team to support and challenge you to achieve your goals, come build your career at United Security!**
